From: Misaka0x272F <324347816+Misaka0x272F@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: fix set_monitor_channel guard for 6.12.101+

Passing net_device to .set_monitor_channel is upstream commit
9c4f830927750a ("wifi: cfg80211: pass net_device to
.set_monitor_channel"), which landed in 6.13.

That commit was backported to the 6.12 stable series as
4dae80dd259b5c24f6c657f434afd5de1f791d12 (committed 2026-08-03) as a
Stable-dep-of 2b0eab425e1f ("wifi: cfg80211: convert pmsr_free_wk to
wiphy_work to fix deadlock").

Verified against include/net/cfg80211.h by tag:

  v6.12        (6.12.0)  -> two arguments
  v6.12.100              -> two arguments
  v6.12.101              -> three arguments (first with the backport)
  v6.12.107              -> three arguments
  v6.13 / v6.14          -> three arguments

The USB driver only tested for >= 6.13, so 6.12.101 through 6.12.x fell
through to the two-argument signature and failed to build:

  error: initialization of
    'int (*)(struct wiphy *, struct net_device *, struct cfg80211_chan_def *)'
  from incompatible pointer type
    'int (*)(struct wiphy *, struct cfg80211_chan_def *)'

Since 6.13 > 6.12.101 the check could be reduced to >= 6.12.101, but
both are kept so the two paths that introduced the signature stay
visible.

The nine parenthesised guards are updated together. The MODULE_IMPORT_NS
guards use the same threshold without parentheses and are unrelated.

Signed-off-by: Misaka0x272F <324347816+Misaka0x272F@users.noreply.github.com>
